      "title": "Stash and Worktree Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Stash and Worktree Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Stash = a stack",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Stack of commits==: `stash@{0}` is the newest",
                "Saves tracked changes from working tree and index",
                "Then resets the tree to `HEAD`",
                "One entry = ==2 or 3 commits==",
                "{red:Local only}: a stash is never pushed"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Working tree",
                    "sub": "commit 1",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Index",
                    "sub": "commit 2",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Untracked",
                    "sub": "optional commit 3",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Worktree = extra checkout",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Extra directory== linked to the same repo",
                "Own checked-out **branch**, `HEAD` and index",
                "One shared `.git` object store and refs",
                "A commit in one is ==instantly visible== in the others"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git worktree add ../hotfix -b fix/login"
              ],
              "note": "new folder, new branch"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which one?",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Stash",
                "Worktree"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Lasts",
                  "Minutes",
                  "Hours or days"
                ],
                [
                  "Checkouts",
                  "One, time-shared",
                  "Many, side by side"
                ],
                [
                  "Holds",
                  "Stack of commits",
                  "Own branch, HEAD, index"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "==Stash== = short interruption you return to in minutes. ==Worktree== = parallel work lasting hours or days."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core Stash Workflow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Core Stash Workflow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Save and list",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git stash push -m \"wip: login form\"` saves ==tracked== changes with a label, cleans the tree",
                "Bare `git stash` does the same, with no message",
                "`git stash list` shows `stash@{0}`, `stash@{1}`, ...: ==newest is always 0=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git stash push -m \"wip: login form\"",
                "git stash list"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "stash@{0}: On main: wip: login form",
                "stash@{1}: WIP on main: 3f2a1 lexer"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Restore",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Applies",
                "Entry after"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git stash pop`",
                  "newest",
                  "{green:dropped} on clean apply; {red:kept} on conflict"
                ],
                [
                  "`git stash apply`",
                  "newest",
                  "kept"
                ],
                [
                  "`git stash apply stash@{1}`",
                  "chosen entry",
                  "kept"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==apply keeps== the entry on the stack",
                "So one stash can go onto ==several branches=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Remove",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git stash drop stash@{n}` deletes ==one== entry",
                "`git stash clear` deletes ==all== entries, no prompt",
                "Drop renumbers only entries below it: dropping `{0}` makes old `{1}` the new `{0}`",
                "Dropping `{1}` leaves `{0}` unchanged"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "pop = apply + drop",
              "text": "Pop drops the entry ==only if the apply succeeded==. Check `git stash list` after a conflict."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Everyday Stash Options",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Everyday Stash Options",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What gets swept up",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Tracked",
                "Untracked",
                "Ignored"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "none",
                  "yes",
                  "no",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`-u`",
                  "yes",
                  "yes",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`-a`",
                  "yes",
                  "yes",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`-u` (`--include-untracked`) stashes new files; plain stash ==silently leaves them== behind",
                "`-a` (`--all`) adds ignored files: can sweep up build output and `.env`, so ==use rarely=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Stash only part",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Pathspec** form stashes only the listed paths",
                "`-p` picks ==hunks== interactively",
                "`--keep-index` stashes but leaves staged changes in the working tree"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git stash push -- path/to/file",
                "git stash push -p",
                "git stash push --keep-index"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Inspect and rescue",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`show -p` prints a stash as a ==diff==",
                "`stash branch` branches from the commit where the stash was made, applies it, then drops it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git stash show -p stash@{0}",
                "git stash branch fix/topic stash@{0}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot -u?",
              "text": "New files stay behind in the tree and can collide on the next branch switch."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Stash Conflicts and Safe Recovery",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Stash Conflicts and Safe Recovery",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. When Pop or Apply Conflicts",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pop or apply onto a ==changed base== can **conflict**",
                "Resolve the files, then `git add` them: ==no commit needed==",
                "`apply` refuses if local changes touch the same files: **commit or stash first**"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Entry Stays",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "git stash pop",
                    "sub": "base changed",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Conflict",
                    "sub": "entry kept",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Resolve + add",
                    "sub": "no commit",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "git stash drop",
                    "sub": "manual",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Duplicate trap",
              "text": "A conflicted pop does ==not drop== the entry. Check `git stash list`, then `git stash drop`, or you reapply it later."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Recover and Escape",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git fsck --unreachable | grep commit",
                "git stash apply <sha>"
              ],
              "note": "a dropped stash is a dangling commit"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git stash branch fix/topic stash@{0}` replays on the ==exact original base commit==",
                "Cleanest way out of **persistent conflicts**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Git Worktree Commands and Choosing Between Them",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Git Worktree Commands and Choosing Between Them",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Worktree Commands",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`add -b` makes a ==new directory + new branch==",
                "A remote-tracking ref gives a **detached HEAD**; add `-b` for a local branch",
                "`list` shows each ==path==, HEAD commit and branch",
                "`remove` deletes a clean worktree; `remove --force` if dirty"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git worktree add ../hotfix -b fix/login",
                "git worktree add ../review -b pr-branch origin/pr-branch",
                "git worktree list",
                "git worktree remove --force ../hotfix"
              ],
              "note": "-b pr-branch gives a local branch tracking the PR"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rules and Cleanup",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One branch lives in ==one worktree== at a time",
                "Git {red:refuses} a second checkout of the same branch",
                "Deleting the folder by hand leaves **stale metadata**",
                "Clean it with `git worktree prune`",
                "Ignored files are not shared: own `node_modules` / venv each"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Worktree or Stash?",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Pick"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Long build or tests while you keep coding",
                  "{green:worktree}"
                ],
                [
                  "Review a PR without touching your work",
                  "{green:worktree}"
                ],
                [
                  "Hotfix mid-feature",
                  "{green:worktree}"
                ],
                [
                  "Quick switch, a few minutes",
                  "{blue:stash}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Worktree = ==parallel work== (hours or days). Stash = a **short interruption** (minutes)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Stash and Worktree Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Stash and Worktree Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Stash commands",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git stash push -m \"msg\"",
                "git stash push -u",
                "git stash push -- path",
                "git stash push -p",
                "git stash list; git stash show -p",
                "git stash apply; git stash pop",
                "git stash drop; git stash clear",
                "git stash branch name"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pop vs apply",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pop` = apply + ==drop== on success",
                "`apply` keeps the entry",
                "A ==conflict== keeps the entry in both cases"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Worktrees",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git worktree add ../hotfix -b fix/login",
                "git worktree add ../review origin/pr-branch",
                "git worktree list",
                "git worktree remove ../hotfix",
                "git worktree prune"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Pitfalls and choice",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Untracked files need `-u`",
                "A stash is never pushed",
                "One branch, one worktree only",
                "A conflicted pop leaves the entry on the stack"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Pick"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Minutes of interruption",
                  "**stash**"
                ],
                [
                  "Hours or parallel work",
                  "**worktree**"
                ],
                [
                  "Stash you cannot finish",
                  "**stash branch**"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`git stash pop` hits a conflict. Is the stash entry still in the list?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Yes: pop drops the entry only after a clean apply",
                "Resolve, `git add`, then `git stash drop` by hand"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You edited `app.py` and created `notes.txt`, then ran `git stash`. What stays on disk?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`notes.txt`: untracked files are skipped",
                "`app.py` is reset to HEAD",
                "`git stash push -u` takes both"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`git worktree add ../x main` fails while main is checked out elsewhere. Why, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "One branch can live in only one worktree",
                "Use `--detach` or `-b new-name main`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You ran `rm -rf ../hotfix` on a linked worktree. What is left behind?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Stale metadata, still listed",
                "Clear it with `git worktree prune`"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}